		{"id":"c3cee3669061ee69","x":360,"y":-3620,"width":940,"height":1300,"type":"text","text":"```json\n{ \"status\": \"success\", \"processed_tables\": [ { \"table_label\": \"General Ledger Sheet1\", \"search_fields\": [ \"context\", \"table_label\", \"embedding_input\" ], \"detailed_input\": [ { \"context\": \"FP&A relies on accurate, standardized, and controlled financial data to support planning, budgeting, forecasting, and management decision-making.\\\\nThe Chart of Accounts defines the enterprise financial structure and classifies all financial activity into consistent, reportable categories.\\\\nEvery account in the Chart of Accounts must be unique, correctly typed (asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense), and aligned to reporting and management hierarchies.\\\\nThe Trial Balance is the primary financial control layer that validates accounting integrity by ensuring total debits equal total credits for a specific period and entity.\\\\nA balanced Trial Balance is the minimum requirement for producing reliable financial statements and performance analysis.\\\\nThe General Ledger stores all transaction-level postings and acts as the single source of truth for actual financial data.\\\\nEvery General Ledger entry must reference a valid account, period, entity, currency, and source document to ensure traceability and audit readiness.\\\\nThese three structures together feed financial statements, variance analysis, management reporting, and forecast models.\\\\nStandardized account structures enable accurate consolidation, cross-entity comparison, and efficient financial close processes.\\\\nPoor data quality in any of these layers leads to incorrect KPIs, misleading forecasts, inaccurate margins, and unreliable cash flow projections.\\\\nFP&A environments require automated, continuous DQ controls covering uniqueness, completeness, validity, referential integrity, hierarchy alignment, timeliness, and mathematical accuracy for these datasets.\\\\nThis context defines the foundation for building scalable, automated DQ frameworks for financial governance and analytics.\" }, { \"table_label\": \"General Ledger Sheet1\" }, { \"embedding_input\": \"[IDENTITY] sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1.test_919_09.test_919_09 | Sample General Ledger Export Cleansed Sheet from test_919_09 source | General Ledger Entries in Financial Planning & Analysis | test_919_09 Finance | aka: gl_export, cleansed_gl_data | [ONTOLOGY] Entity: General Ledger Entry | Parent: Financial Account.account_number (1:M) | Children: None | Related: Trial Balance via account_number; Financial Statement via document_number | Domain: Finance | Role: transactional | [SEMANTICS] Table for storing cleansed transaction-level postings including account details, amounts, and associated metadata | Purpose: supports financial reporting, variance analysis, and management decision-making | Rules: account_number must exist in Chart of Accounts; total debits must equal total credits; document_number must be unique; date must be within reporting period | Dependencies: if amount_foreign_currency exists then exchange_rate must be provided; if department_id is specified then department must exist | Standards: financial reporting standards | [TECHNICAL] transactional | Columns: 28 | PK: line_unique_key | FK: account_number→chart_of_accounts.account_number, department_id→departments.department_id, subsidiary_id→subsidiaries.subsidiary_id | Indexes: idx_account_number, idx_date, idx_document_number | Format: structured data\" } ], \"search_query\": \"What are the key components and processes involved in managing transaction-level financial data for accurate reporting and analysis in a General Ledger, including the importance of account classification, balance validation, and compliance with financial reporting standards?\", \"semantic_results\": [ { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359a\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3599\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3598\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359f\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359e\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359b\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359c\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359d\", \"concept_name\": \"\" } ], \"selected_concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359a\", \"binding_success\": true, \"error\": null }, { \"table_label\": \"Chart of Accounts Hierarchy Format\", \"search_fields\": [ \"context\", \"table_label\", \"embedding_input\" ], \"detailed_input\": [ { \"context\": \"FP&A relies on accurate, standardized, and controlled financial data to support planning, budgeting, forecasting, and management decision-making.\\\\nThe Chart of Accounts defines the enterprise financial structure and classifies all financial activity into consistent, reportable categories.\\\\nEvery account in the Chart of Accounts must be unique, correctly typed (asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense), and aligned to reporting and management hierarchies.\\\\nThe Trial Balance is the primary financial control layer that validates accounting integrity by ensuring total debits equal total credits for a specific period and entity.\\\\nA balanced Trial Balance is the minimum requirement for producing reliable financial statements and performance analysis.\\\\nThe General Ledger stores all transaction-level postings and acts as the single source of truth for actual financial data.\\\\nEvery General Ledger entry must reference a valid account, period, entity, currency, and source document to ensure traceability and audit readiness.\\\\nThese three structures together feed financial statements, variance analysis, management reporting, and forecast models.\\\\nStandardized account structures enable accurate consolidation, cross-entity comparison, and efficient financial close processes.\\\\nPoor data quality in any of these layers leads to incorrect KPIs, misleading forecasts, inaccurate margins, and unreliable cash flow projections.\\\\nFP&A environments require automated, continuous DQ controls covering uniqueness, completeness, validity, referential integrity, hierarchy alignment, timeliness, and mathematical accuracy for these datasets.\\\\nThis context defines the foundation for building scalable, automated DQ frameworks for financial governance and analytics.\" }, { \"table_label\": \"Chart of Accounts Hierarchy Format\" }, { \"embedding_input\": \"[IDENTITY] coa_hierarchy_format_in.test_919_09.test_919_09 | Chart of Accounts Hierarchy Format Input from test_919_09 source | Financial Accounts in Financial Planning & Analysis | test_919_09 Finance | aka: coa_hierarchy, account_structure, financial_account_hierarchy | [ONTOLOGY] Entity: Financial Account | Parent: None | Children: None | Related: Trial Balance via account classification | Domain: Finance | Role: master | [SEMANTICS] Master table for defining the hierarchy and structure of financial accounts including account names, aliases, and parent-child relationships | Purpose: support account classification and reporting hierarchy for financial data | Rules: member_id must be unique; external_id must be valid; parent_name must reference existing member_name; member_alias must be unique if provided | Dependencies: if operator='add' then cmd must specify valid operation; if member_alias is provided then member_name must be unique | Standards: Financial reporting standards | [TECHNICAL] master | Columns: 8 | PK: member_id | FK: account_number→external_systems.account_number | Indexes: idx_member_id, idx_parent_name | Format: structured data\" } ], \"search_query\": \"Search for concepts related to the hierarchical structure and classification of financial accounts, including account names and relationships, that support accurate financial reporting and analysis in financial planning and analysis environments.\", \"semantic_results\": [ { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3598\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359f\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359e\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359a\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359c\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3599\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359b\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359d\", \"concept_name\": \"\" } ], \"selected_concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3598\", \"binding_success\": true, \"error\": null }, { \"table_label\": \"Trial Balance Sheet1\", \"search_fields\": [ \"context\", \"table_label\", \"embedding_input\" ], \"detailed_input\": [ { \"context\": \"FP&A relies on accurate, standardized, and controlled financial data to support planning, budgeting, forecasting, and management decision-making.\\\\nThe Chart of Accounts defines the enterprise financial structure and classifies all financial activity into consistent, reportable categories.\\\\nEvery account in the Chart of Accounts must be unique, correctly typed (asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense), and aligned to reporting and management hierarchies.\\\\nThe Trial Balance is the primary financial control layer that validates accounting integrity by ensuring total debits equal total credits for a specific period and entity.\\\\nA balanced Trial Balance is the minimum requirement for producing reliable financial statements and performance analysis.\\\\nThe General Ledger stores all transaction-level postings and acts as the single source of truth for actual financial data.\\\\nEvery General Ledger entry must reference a valid account, period, entity, currency, and source document to ensure traceability and audit readiness.\\\\nThese three structures together feed financial statements, variance analysis, management reporting, and forecast models.\\\\nStandardized account structures enable accurate consolidation, cross-entity comparison, and efficient financial close processes.\\\\nPoor data quality in any of these layers leads to incorrect KPIs, misleading forecasts, inaccurate margins, and unreliable cash flow projections.\\\\nFP&A environments require automated, continuous DQ controls covering uniqueness, completeness, validity, referential integrity, hierarchy alignment, timeliness, and mathematical accuracy for these datasets.\\\\nThis context defines the foundation for building scalable, automated DQ frameworks for financial governance and analytics.\" }, { \"table_label\": \"Trial Balance Sheet1\" }, { \"embedding_input\": \"[IDENTITY] sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1.test_919_09.test_919_09 | Sample Trial Balance Export Table from test_919_09 source | Trial Balance in Financial Planning & Analysis | test_919_09 Finance | aka: tb_export, trial_balance_data | [ONTOLOGY] Entity: Trial Balance | Parent: Financial Account.account_number (1:M) | Children: None | Related: General Ledger via account_number | Domain: Finance | Role: master | [SEMANTICS] Table for capturing trial balance data including account numbers, subsidiaries, and financial metrics over time | Purpose: validate accounting integrity, support financial reporting and analysis | Rules: account_number must be unique; subsidiary_id must exist in subsidiaries; total debits must equal total credits; event_id must be unique | Dependencies: if reporting_period='current' then all entries must reference valid accounts; if subsidiary_id is null then activity must be flagged | Standards: Financial reporting standards | [TECHNICAL] master | Columns: 15 | PK: account_number, event_id | FK: subsidiary_id→subsidiaries.subsidiary_id | Indexes: idx_account_number, idx_event_id | Format: structured data\" } ], \"search_query\": \"What is the role of the Trial Balance in ensuring accounting integrity and supporting accurate financial reporting and analysis within the financial planning and analysis framework?\", \"semantic_results\": [ { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3599\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359a\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3598\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359e\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359f\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359b\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359c\", \"concept_name\": \"\" }, { \"concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f359d\", \"concept_name\": \"\" } ], \"selected_concept_id\": \"6944155b3b0093f1628f3599\", \"binding_success\": true, \"error\": null } ] }\n```"}
